work-order.text:
{
  "acceptance": [
    {
      "check": "Group page shows every member's net balance and a simplified who-pays-whom list with at most N-1 transfers, a group with no debts shows an explicit settled all-zero state, and an archived group renders the reads with no settle-up or delete controls",
      "id": "AC-1"
    },
    {
      "check": "Home shows the viewer's cross-group you-owe and you-are-owed totals plus per-person rows plus each group's per-group balance in its own currency, with a note naming excluded foreign-currency groups",
      "id": "AC-2"
    },
    {
      "check": "A member records a full and a partial settle-up payment from the debts card behind a confirm, deletes a payment as an involved member behind a confirm, and a non-involved member's delete is refused; balances update in place with a polite live-region announcement",
      "id": "AC-3"
    },
    {
      "check": "Every amount on both screens renders in group currency through formatMinorUnits with tabular numerals, and the debts card sits above the expense list on a narrow viewport",
      "id": "AC-4"
    },
    {
      "check": "The debts card renders a persistent polite live region (role=status) from first paint, so the first settle-up and delete results are announced as updates to an already-present region rather than as a region inserted together with its message",
      "id": "AC-9"
    }
  ],
  "approach": "Fix the shared contract the previous plan miscopied instead of reworking payments: drop the idle early-return in components/ui.tsx StateMessage so it always renders its region — idle renders an empty <p role=status aria-live=polite>, success renders the message in that same node, error keeps role=alert unchanged. No logic change in components/settle-panels.tsx is needed: both panels already mount StateMessage unconditionally at panel level, so their regions become persistent automatically. Add components/ui.test.tsx with the idle-renders-empty-region repro plus success/error cases. Append AC-9 plus a qa_script step so QA asserts pre-submit region presence on every future run.",
  "files": [
    {
      "action": "edit",
      "change": "Drop the idle/message-empty early null return in StateMessage so it always renders its region: idle yields an empty <p role=status aria-live=polite>, success renders the message in that same node, error keeps role=alert unchanged",
      "path": "components/ui.tsx",
      "why": "The shared live-region contract every panel mounts"
    }
  ],
  "issue": 7,
  "kind": "bug",
  "mode": "committed",
  "reproduced": true,
  "root_cause": "components/ui.tsx StateMessage returns null while idle, so both settle panels mount with zero live regions from first paint; the first result inserts the [aria-live] node together with its message, which screen readers announce unreliably. The previous work order assumed the ConfirmStep-plus-StateMessage pattern is a persistent live region; it never was.",
  "understanding": "PR #22 implemented the previous plan faithfully and still failed QA because the plan's premise was wrong, not its execution. The plan treated ConfirmStep-plus-StateMessage as a persistent live region, but StateMessage returns null while idle (components/ui.tsx:34), so the debts card mounts zero [aria-live] nodes until the first submit — exactly what T-12 asserts against (BUG-1). The ledger, balances, simplification, authz, payments and responsive work all passed (12/13). My previous revision was additionally refused by the validator for dropping IAC/TR sources; this revision restores AC-1 through AC-8 verbatim with sources and appends AC-9.",
  "version": 2
}
